{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nThe task is AGENT-TF-01: implement `solve(case)` that filters API calls based on normalized gain.\n\nFrom the candidate artifact description:\n- For each call: gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call\n- Normalize gain by prediction_tokens (divide by prediction_tokens)\n- Accept if parseable=true AND normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\n- Return accepted_call_ids and diagnostics (in supplied call order)\n\nThe output schema requires:\n- `accepted_call_ids`: array of strings\n- `diagnostics`: array of objects with `accepted` (bool), `call_id` (string), `normalized_gain` (number)\n\nLet me verify with the first fixture:\n- threshold = 0.05\n- call0: loss_without=1.48911432, loss_with=0.30132987, tokens=5, parseable=true\n  - gain = 1.48911432 - 0.30132987 = 1.18778445\n  - normalized = 1.18778445 / 5 = 0.23755689\n  - accepted: parseable=true and 0.237 \u003e= 0.05 → true\n\n- call5: parseable=false → not accepted\n\nSo the algorithm is straightforward. Let me write the Python code:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    diagnostics = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / tokens\n        \n        accepted = parseable and normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"normalized_gain\": round(normalized_gain, 10),  # or some rounding\n            \"accepted\": accepted\n        })\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nThe artifact says \"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\" I need to think about what rounding to apply. Let me just use standard floating point without explicit rounding, or round to a reasonable number of decimal places. The schema says `normalized_gain` is a `number` type, so any float works.\n\nActually, I'll keep it as a float without explicit rounding since the schema just requires a number type.\n\nNow format this as a JSON response with the implementation key.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n    diagnostics = []\\n\\n    for call in calls:\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / tokens\\n\\n        accepted = bool(parseable and normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\\n\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain,\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted\\n        })\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01Qfbs49mPqYt13HWNhwAIsu","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2363},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2363,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":19,"output_tokens":873,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":625},"service_tier":"standard"}}